{
  "_comment": "Copy to managed-settings.fragment.json to add THIS deployment's rules to Axon's managed Claude Code policy. Applied by `tools/claude-code-config --managed`, which merges it over tools/templates/claude-code/managed-settings.json and deploys the result to /etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json. Delete this file if the machine needs no additions — an absent fragment is the normal case, not an error.",
  "_contract": "RESTRICTIVE ONLY. The merge accepts only validated entries under permissions.deny, sandbox.filesystem.denyRead/denyWrite, and sandbox.credentials.files/envVars. Allowlist additions, new keys, scalar changes, replacements, and removals are hard errors that deploy nothing.",
  "_why_here": "What belongs in a fragment is anything true of this deployment rather than of Axon: the credential env vars that exist on this machine, paths only this boundary has, an employer's internal hosts. Axon is public at every commit (RULES.md Rule 21), so that inventory cannot live there. Names and paths only — never a secret VALUE (Rule 13).",
  "_removing": "Keys prefixed with _ are documentation and are stripped before deploy; keep or delete them freely.",

  "permissions": {
    "deny": [
      "Read(~/Protected/**)",
      "Edit(~/Protected/**)"
    ]
  },
  "sandbox": {
    "filesystem": {
      "denyRead": ["~/Protected/**"],
      "denyWrite": ["~/Protected/**"]
    },
    "credentials": {
      "envVars": [
        {
          "name": "EXAMPLE_INTERNAL_API_KEY",
          "mode": "deny"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
